# Correction Task: Wire Up New Services and Complete Integration

## Found
The previous implementation created 9 new files (services, base classes) and registered them in DI, but **did not refactor the existing code to actually use them**. The new services sit unused while all the original duplicated code remains intact. Additionally:
- `PromptParser.cs` has a regex bug on lines 96 and 196
- `BaseQueueItem` was created but queue item models don't extend it
- `NavigationService` was created but code-behind files still use manual navigation
- `WorkflowNodeUpdater` was created but ViewModels still do inline JSON manipulation
- Phase 5 (UserControls + accessibility) was not attempted

## Fix Required
This correction task focuses on the **integration work** — making the existing code use the new services. It is split into 4 parts. **Build after each part with `dotnet build FlipPix.sln` and fix any errors before continuing.**

---

## Part A — Bug Fix + Queue Item Migration

### A1. Fix PromptParser Regex Bug
In `FlipPix.UI/Services/PromptParser.cs`:

**Line 96** — Replace:
```csharp
cleaned = Regex.Replace(cleaned, @"^[ chronology\*\•\-]+[\s\)]*", "", RegexOptions.IgnoreCase);
```
With:
```csharp
cleaned = Regex.Replace(cleaned, @"^[\s\*\•\-]+[\s\)]*", "");
```

**Line 196** — Replace:
```csharp
var pattern = @"^[ chronology\*\•\-]+(.+)$";
```
With:
```csharp
var pattern = @"^[\s\*\•\-]+(.+)$";
```

### A2. Migrate Queue Item Models to Extend BaseQueueItem
The `BaseQueueItem` class (in `FlipPix.UI/Models/BaseQueueItem.cs`) already provides: `Id`, `CreatedAt`, `StartedAt`, `CompletedAt`, `ErrorMessage`, `Status`, `Progress`, `OutputImagePath`, `ThumbnailImage`, `OpenImageCommand`, `StatusDisplay`, `StatusColor`, `LoadThumbnail()`, `OpenImage()`, `OnPropertyChanged()`.

For each queue item model listed below, **remove** the properties/methods/fields already defined in `BaseQueueItem` and change the class to extend `BaseQueueItem` instead of implementing `INotifyPropertyChanged` directly.

#### `FlipPix.UI/Models/ImagePromptQueueItem.cs`
1. Change `public class ImagePromptQueueItem : INotifyPropertyChanged` → `public class ImagePromptQueueItem : BaseQueueItem`
2. Remove these members (they're now inherited from BaseQueueItem):
   - Fields: `_status`, `_progress`, `_outputImagePath`, `_thumbnailImage`
   - Properties: `Id`, `OutputImagePath`, `HasOutputImage` (add back as `public bool HasOutputImage => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(OutputImagePath);` since BaseQueueItem doesn't have this), `ThumbnailImage`, `OpenImageCommand`, `CreatedAt`, `StartedAt`, `CompletedAt`, `ErrorMessage`, `Status`, `Progress`, `StatusDisplay`, `StatusColor`, `DisplayPrompt` (keep this — it's unique)
   - Methods: `LoadThumbnail()`, `OpenImage()`, `OnPropertyChanged()`
   - Event: `PropertyChanged`
3. Keep only: `Prompt`, `AspectRatioIndex`, `Steps`, `Cfg`, `Seed`, `Denoise`, `LoraEnabled`, `SelectedLora`, `SelectedWorkflow`, `DisplayPrompt`, `HasOutputImage`
4. Update the constructor — remove `OpenImageCommand = new RelayCommand(...)` since the base class constructor handles it. Call `base()` implicitly.

#### `FlipPix.UI/Models/StoryPromptItem.cs`
1. Change `public class StoryPromptItem : INotifyPropertyChanged` → `public class StoryPromptItem : BaseQueueItem`
2. Remove inherited members (same as above — `_status`, `_progress`, `_outputImagePath`, `_thumbnailImage`, `Status`, `Progress`, `OutputImagePath`, `ThumbnailImage`, `OpenImageCommand`, `CreatedAt`, `StartedAt`, `CompletedAt`, `ErrorMessage`, `LoadThumbnail()`, `OpenImage()`, `OnPropertyChanged()`, `PropertyChanged`)
3. Keep only: `Index`, `Prompt`, `InputImagePath`, `StyleName`, `StyleWorkflowFile`, `LoraEnabled`, `SelectedLora`, `LoraStrengthModel`, `LoraStrengthClip`, `SelectedStyle`, `SpicyContentEnabled`, `NegativePrompt`, `SelectedOrientation`
4. Remove the `using CommunityToolkit.Mvvm.Input;` import if no longer needed (check if RelayCommand is still used).

#### `FlipPix.UI/Models/CameraQueueItem.cs`
Same pattern — extend `BaseQueueItem`, remove duplicated members, keep only camera-specific properties.

#### `FlipPix.UI/Models/ImageAnalyzerQueueItem.cs`
Same pattern — extend `BaseQueueItem`, remove duplicated members, keep only analyzer-specific properties.

#### `FlipPix.UI/Models/QueueItem.cs`
Same pattern — extend `BaseQueueItem`, remove duplicated members, keep only video-specific properties.

#### `FlipPix.UI/Models/StoryVideoQueueItem.cs`
Same pattern — extend `BaseQueueItem`, remove duplicated members, keep only story-video-specific properties.

**IMPORTANT**: Some models use `"Queued"` as default status instead of `"Pending"`. If so, set `Status = "Queued"` in the subclass constructor after calling `base()`.

**IMPORTANT**: Some models may have slightly different `StatusDisplay` or `StatusColor` switch values. The `BaseQueueItem` already handles `"Pending"`, `"Queued"`, `"Processing"`, `"Completed"`, `"Failed"`, `"Cancelled"`. If a subclass needs additional statuses, override the property.

**Build and fix any compilation errors before proceeding to Part B.**

