## Part B — Wire Up WorkflowNodeUpdater in Story Generators

The `WorkflowNodeUpdater` static class (in `FlipPix.UI/Services/WorkflowNodeUpdater.cs`) provides:
```csharp
public static void UpdateNodeInput(ref string workflowJson, string nodeId, string inputName, object value)
public static void UpdateNodeInputMultiple(ref string workflowJson, string nodeId, Dictionary<string, object> inputs)
```

### B1. Refactor `StoryImageGeneratorQViewModel.cs` — `UpdateWorkflowParameters` (lines ~166-277)
The current code deserializes workflow JSON into `Dictionary<string, JsonElement>`, manually navigates to nodes, and updates inputs. Replace with `WorkflowNodeUpdater` calls.

Current pattern (repeated for each node):
```csharp
var workflowObj = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>(workflowJson);
// ... manual node manipulation
workflowJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(workflowObj);
```

Replace with:
```csharp
WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInput(ref workflowJson, "213", "image", inputImageFilename);
WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInput(ref workflowJson, "153", "text", positivePrompt);
WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInput(ref workflowJson, "154", "text", negativePrompt);
WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInputMultiple(ref workflowJson, "3", new Dictionary<string, object>
{
    { "steps", steps },
    { "cfg", cfg },
    { "seed", seed }
});
WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInput(ref workflowJson, "145", "shift", shift);
WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInput(ref workflowJson, "218", "filename_prefix", filenamePrefix);
```

Adapt the exact node IDs and input names from the existing code. Keep any conditional logic (e.g., "only set LoRA if enabled") intact.

### B2. Refactor `StoryImageGeneratorFViewModel.cs` — `UpdateWorkflowParameters` (lines ~195-292)
Same approach. Node IDs for this workflow:
- Node 148: LoadImage → `image`
- Node 154: TextEncodeEditAdvanced → `text` (prompt)
- Node 109: Flux2Scheduler → `steps`
- Node 157: SaveImage → `filename_prefix`, `subfolder`
- Node 115: ImageScale → `width`, `height`

### B3. Refactor `StoryImageGeneratorAmateurViewModel.cs` — `UpdateWorkflowParameters` (lines ~273-434)
Same approach. Node IDs for this workflow:
- Node 6: Positive prompt
- Node 7: Negative prompt
- Node 28: Seed
- Nodes 582, 620: ClownsharKSampler (cfg, steps)
- Nodes 754, 768: KSampler (denoise values)
- Nodes 105, 752: LoRA strength
- Node 760: Character LoRA
- Latent nodes 46, 693, 758, 772: dimensions

### B4. Refactor `StoryImageGeneratorViewModel.cs` (Z variant) — `UpdateWorkflowParameters` (lines ~577-769)
Same approach. Node IDs for this workflow:
- Node 385: StringTrim (user prompt)
- Node 60: Negative prompt
- Node 307: Seed
- Node 125: Style template
- Node 9: Output filename prefix
- Node 56: EmptyLatentImage (width/height)
- Nodes 243, 248: SD3 width/height

**Keep** the LoRA foreach loop logic — it iterates Power Lora Loader nodes dynamically. Just replace the individual node updates with `WorkflowNodeUpdater` calls.

### B5. Refactor Video ViewModels (if they have similar patterns)
Check `LTX2AudioViewModel.cs`, `MochaVideoViewModel.cs`, `VACEVideoViewModel.cs` for `UpdateWorkflowParameters` or equivalent methods. If they do the same `Dictionary<string, JsonElement>` pattern, refactor to use `WorkflowNodeUpdater`.

**Build and fix any compilation errors before proceeding to Part C.**

