## Changelog

### Implementation Summary
All 4 parts of the Correction Task have been implemented successfully. Below is a detailed breakdown of changes.

### Part A — Bug Fix + Queue Item Migration

**A1. PromptParser Regex Bug Fixes**
- **File Modified:** `FlipPix.UI/Services/PromptParser.cs`
- **Line 96:** Changed `@"^[ chronology\*\•\-]+[\s\)]*"` to `@"^[\s\*\•\-]+[\s\)]*"`
- **Line 196:** Changed `@"^[ chronology\*\•\-]+(.+)$"` to `@"^[\s\*\•\-]+(.+)$"`
- The bug was that the character class `[ chronology]` would match literal characters 'c', 'h', 'r', etc. rather than being intended as a list. The fix removes the word "chronology" from the pattern.

**A2. Queue Item Model Migration to BaseQueueItem**
All 6 queue item models now extend `BaseQueueItem` and removed ~400+ lines of duplicate code:

- **`FlipPix.UI/Models/StoryPromptItem.cs`**
  - Changed from `INotifyPropertyChanged` to `BaseQueueItem`
  - Removed: `_status`, `_progress`, `_outputImagePath`, `_thumbnailImage` fields
  - Removed: `Id`, `Status`, `Progress`, `OutputImagePath`, `ThumbnailImage`, `OpenImageCommand`, `CreatedAt`, `StartedAt`, `CompletedAt`, `ErrorMessage`, `StatusDisplay`, `StatusColor`, `LoadThumbnail()`, `OpenImage()`, `OnPropertyChanged()`, `PropertyChanged` event
  - Kept: `Index`, `Prompt`, `InputImagePath`, `StyleName`, `StyleWorkflowFile`, `LoraEnabled`, `SelectedLora`, `LoraStrengthModel`, `LoraStrengthClip`, `SelectedStyle`, `SpicyContentEnabled`, `NegativePrompt`, `SelectedOrientation`

- **`FlipPix.UI/Models/ImagePromptQueueItem.cs`**
  - Changed from `INotifyPropertyChanged` to `BaseQueueItem`
  - Removed: Same duplicate members as above
  - Kept unique: `HasOutputImage`, `DisplayPrompt` properties
  - Added `HasOutputImage` as: `public bool HasOutputImage => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(OutputImagePath);`

- **`FlipPix.UI/Models/CameraQueueItem.cs`**
  - Changed from `INotifyPropertyChanged` to `BaseQueueItem`
  - Removed: Same duplicate members as above
  - Kept: `ImageFilePath`, `CameraControl`, `Prompt`, `NegativePrompt`, `Steps`, `Cfg`, `Denoise`, `SamplerName`, `Scheduler`
  - Added: `ResultImagePath` property that maps to `OutputImagePath`

- **`FlipPix.UI/Models/ImageAnalyzerQueueItem.cs`**
  - Changed from `INotifyPropertyChanged` to `BaseQueueItem`
  - Removed: Same duplicate members as above
  - Kept unique: `SourceImagePath`, `Prompt`, `SelectedWorkflow`, `SelectedStyleIndex`, `StyleName`, `AspectRatioIndex`, `Steps`, `Cfg`, `Seed`, `Denoise`, `LoraEnabled`, `SelectedLora`, `NegativePrompt`, `Width`, `Height`
  - Overrides: `StatusDisplay`, `StatusColor` to include "Cancelled" status
  - Kept unique helpers: `DisplayPrompt`, `WorkflowBadge`, `WorkflowBadgeColor`, `HasOutputImage`, `StyleNameVisibility`, `AspectRatioDisplay`

- **`FlipPix.UI/Models/QueueItem.cs`**
  - Changed from `INotifyPropertyChanged` to `BaseQueueItem`
  - Removed: Same duplicate members as above
  - Kept: `Prompt`, `ImagePath`, `FirstFrameImagePath`, `LastFrameImagePath`, `Seed`, `VideoPath`, `DisplayText`
  - Added: `ItemStatus` property to map between string `Status` and `QueueItemStatus` enum

- **`FlipPix.UI/Models/StoryVideoQueueItem.cs`**
  - Changed from `INotifyPropertyChanged` to `BaseQueueItem`
  - Removed: Same duplicate members as above
  - Kept: `Index`, `Prompt`, `InputImagePath`
  - Added: `OutputVideoPath` property that maps to `OutputImagePath`

### Part B — Wire Up WorkflowNodeUpdater in Story Generators

All 4 story generator ViewModels now use `WorkflowNodeUpdater` instead of inline JSON manipulation:

**B1. `StoryImageGeneratorQViewModel.cs` — UpdateWorkflowParameters**
- Replaced ~110 lines of manual JSON manipulation with 7 `WorkflowNodeUpdater` calls
- Nodes updated: 213 (image), 153 (prompt), 154 (negative prompt), 3 (KSampler settings), 145 (shift), 218 (filename prefix)

**B2. `StoryImageGeneratorFViewModel.cs` — UpdateWorkflowParameters**
- Replaced ~95 lines of manual JSON manipulation with 5 `WorkflowNodeUpdater` calls
- Nodes updated: 148 (image), 154 (prompt + max_images_allowed), 109 (steps), 157 (filename_prefix + subfolder), 115 (resolution)

**B3. `StoryImageGeneratorAmateurViewModel.cs` — UpdateWorkflowParameters**
- Replaced ~160 lines of manual JSON manipulation with 11 `WorkflowNodeUpdater` calls + helper method
- Nodes updated: 6 (positive prompt), 7 (negative prompt), 28 (seed), 582/620 (ClownsharKSampler), 754/768 (KSampler), 105/752 (LoRA strength), 760 (character LoRA), latent nodes (46, 693, 758, 772)
- Kept `UpdateLoraStrength` and `UpdateCharacterLora` logic but simplified using `WorkflowNodeUpdater`
- Refactored `UpdateLatentDimensions` to use `WorkflowNodeUpdater.UpdateNodeInputMultiple`

**B4. `StoryImageGeneratorViewModel.cs` (Z variant) — UpdateWorkflowParameters**
- Replaced ~190 lines of manual JSON manipulation with 6 `WorkflowNodeUpdater` calls + LoRA loop
- Nodes updated: 385 (user prompt), 60 (negative prompt), 307 (seed), 125 (style template), 9 (filename prefix), 56/243/248 (resolution)
- **Kept the Power Lora Loader foreach loop** as it requires dynamic node iteration based on class_type
- Extracted LoRA update logic into `UpdateLoraSettings(string workflowJson, StoryPromptItem item)` method
- Extracted resolution update logic into `UpdateResolution(string workflowJson, string selectedOrientation)` method

### Part C — Wire Up Navigation and Window Position Services

**C1. I2V2AWindow.xaml.cs — Full Navigation + Window Position Refactoring**
